.SH NAME
anpu-search - Find a security tool by name or keyword


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBanpu search [query] [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Search ranked tools. Each tool has its own --enable/--disable/--only name.

.PP
Levels: safe (1, passive), advanced (2, polite active), ultra (3, intrusive)

.PP
Examples:
  anpu search dns
  anpu search cloud
  anpu search --level ultra
  anpu search --level safe
  anpu tools   # full ranked list


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for search

.PP
\fB--level\fP=""
	filter by level: safe, advanced, ultra


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to a YAML config file (default: anpu.yaml in the current directory, if present)

.PP
\fB--data-dir\fP=""
	data directory for the scan-history DB and caches (default: os.UserConfigDir()/anpu; override with the ANPU_HOME environment variable)

.PP
\fB--verbose\fP[=false]
	show per-stage finding and warning counts


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBanpu(1)\fP


